# Commit message style

Use [Google-style](https://google.github.io/eng-practices/review/developer/cl-descriptions.html) commit messages.

## Format

```
Short imperative summary

Optional body explaining why the change exists, what a reviewer
needs to know, and any follow-ups. Wrap near 72 characters.
```

## Rules

- Subject line: imperative mood ("Add", "Fix", "Ignore"), not past tense
- Subject: concise; aim for ~50 characters when practical
- Blank line between subject and body when a body is present
- Body focuses on **why** and impact, not a file-by-file changelog
- No trailing period on the subject line
- Avoid Conventional Commit prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`) unless explicitly requested

## Examples

```
Add fixture acquisition into data/raw

Copy the tiny corpus from tests/fixtures so Phase 1 can use a
stable raw layout without downloading large datasets locally.
```

```
Ignore setuptools egg-info artifacts

Editable installs generate package metadata that should stay local.
```
